1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:00,950
Lucas…

2
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:01,550
it's me.

3
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:03,450
Sorry, I know it's late.

4
00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:07,150
I found her.

5
00:00:07,220 --> 00:00:08,850
She's in every single photo.

6
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:12,350
And she knows…

7
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:13,650
that I know.

8
00:00:16,300 --> 00:00:20,010
That was the last message Rafael left

9
00:00:20,060 --> 00:00:21,520
on his brother's phone.

10
00:00:21,750 --> 00:00:23,700
At three forty in the morning.

11
00:00:26,780 --> 00:00:28,740
When Lucas got there the next morning,

12
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:30,610
the apartment door was locked from the

13
00:00:30,660 --> 00:00:31,640
inside.

14
00:00:35,310 --> 00:00:37,700
And Rafael was gone.

15
00:00:44,440 --> 00:00:45,360
Good evening.

16
00:00:45,890 --> 00:00:48,300
Welcome back to The Last Shelter.

17
00:00:49,410 --> 00:00:50,360
Tell me something.

18
00:00:50,720 --> 00:00:51,620
And be honest.

19
00:00:52,060 --> 00:00:53,480
Have you ever felt…

20
00:00:53,980 --> 00:00:55,960
someone walking behind you?

21
00:00:56,340 --> 00:00:57,980
Inside your own home?

22
00:00:59,040 --> 00:01:00,800
That chill in the hallway.

23
00:01:01,120 --> 00:01:03,170
That certainty that if you turn around

24
00:01:03,220 --> 00:01:06,330
right now, someone will be there.

25
00:01:07,440 --> 00:01:08,510
So you turn around.

26
00:01:08,560 --> 00:01:10,920
And there's no one.

27
00:01:12,110 --> 00:01:13,560
Everyone has felt it.

28
00:01:14,170 --> 00:01:16,170
And tonight, I'm going to tell you

29
00:01:16,220 --> 00:01:18,190
about a man who decided to find

30
00:01:18,240 --> 00:01:19,400
out why.

31
00:01:20,640 --> 00:01:22,150
In twenty fourteen,

32
00:01:22,200 --> 00:01:24,650
in Switzerland, a group of scientists ran

33
00:01:24,700 --> 00:01:26,420
a strange experiment.

34
00:01:26,940 --> 00:01:29,690
Volunteers were blindfolded and moved a robotic

35
00:01:29,740 --> 00:01:31,480
arm in front of their bodies.

36
00:01:31,860 --> 00:01:33,070
And a second robot,

37
00:01:33,120 --> 00:01:35,300
behind them, touched their backs.

38
00:01:35,760 --> 00:01:37,320
With a half-second delay.

39
00:01:38,270 --> 00:01:40,610
Many of them began to feel someone

40
00:01:40,660 --> 00:01:42,280
standing behind them.

41
00:01:42,500 --> 00:01:43,920
Some counted two,

42
00:01:44,080 --> 00:01:46,360
three, four presences.

43
00:01:47,090 --> 00:01:48,860
Some begged them to stop.

44
00:01:50,120 --> 00:01:52,560
The scientists' conclusion was simple:

45
00:01:52,980 --> 00:01:53,920
it's the brain.

46
00:01:54,220 --> 00:01:56,740
A delay between what the body does

47
00:01:57,140 --> 00:01:58,440
and what it feels.

48
00:01:59,270 --> 00:02:00,160
Nothing more.

49
00:02:01,280 --> 00:02:02,280
Nothing more.

50
00:02:05,020 --> 00:02:07,130
Rafael was thirty-four.

51
00:02:07,180 --> 00:02:08,360
A sound engineer.

52
00:02:08,680 --> 00:02:10,470
He lived alone in an old apartment,

53
00:02:10,520 --> 00:02:12,320
on the third floor,

54
00:02:12,420 --> 00:02:14,220
at the end of a quiet street.

55
00:02:15,650 --> 00:02:17,620
And ever since he was a child,

56
00:02:18,240 --> 00:02:19,420
he had felt it.

57
00:02:20,150 --> 00:02:22,070
The first time was at his grandmother's

58
00:02:22,120 --> 00:02:23,740
house, in the countryside.

59
00:02:23,920 --> 00:02:25,150
A long hallway,

60
00:02:25,200 --> 00:02:26,770
with creaking floorboards,

61
00:02:26,820 --> 00:02:28,450
that ran from the kitchen to the

62
00:02:28,500 --> 00:02:29,300
bedrooms.

63
00:02:29,880 --> 00:02:30,980
He was about seven.

64
00:02:31,420 --> 00:02:33,810
Every night, he ran down that hallway,

65
00:02:33,860 --> 00:02:36,220
certain that someone was coming after him.

66
00:02:37,200 --> 00:02:39,080
Once, he told his grandmother.

67
00:02:39,740 --> 00:02:40,700
She didn't laugh.

68
00:02:41,180 --> 00:02:42,810
She just held his face in both

69
00:02:42,860 --> 00:02:44,440
hands and said,

70
00:02:44,630 --> 00:02:48,430
very seriously: Don't look for it,

71
00:02:48,480 --> 00:02:49,280
child.

72
00:02:49,800 --> 00:02:51,100
If you don't look…

73
00:02:51,750 --> 00:02:53,100
you won't find.

74
00:02:54,740 --> 00:02:56,480
He never understood what she meant.

75
00:02:56,840 --> 00:02:58,680
Not until many years later.

76
00:03:00,050 --> 00:03:01,740
At first, it was rare.

77
00:03:02,270 --> 00:03:02,970
Every now and then,

78
00:03:03,020 --> 00:03:05,910
watching TV, he'd feel someone's eyes on

79
00:03:05,960 --> 00:03:07,180
the back of his neck.

80
00:03:07,840 --> 00:03:09,830
But it was in the hallway that

81
00:03:09,880 --> 00:03:11,200
it truly began.

82
00:03:12,330 --> 00:03:14,210
The apartment had a long hallway,

83
00:03:14,260 --> 00:03:16,300
from the living room to the bedroom.

84
00:03:16,870 --> 00:03:18,530
And every time he walked down it

85
00:03:18,580 --> 00:03:20,670
at night, he felt someone coming up

86
00:03:20,720 --> 00:03:21,760
behind him.

87
00:03:22,520 --> 00:03:23,920
He would stop.

88
00:03:24,860 --> 00:03:26,580
The silence stopped with him.

89
00:03:27,810 --> 00:03:29,620
And every time he turned around…

90
00:03:30,320 --> 00:03:32,080
the hallway was empty.

91
00:03:33,420 --> 00:03:34,820
Try something right now.

92
00:03:35,590 --> 00:03:36,740
Don't look behind you.

93
00:03:37,600 --> 00:03:38,830
Just pay attention to the back of

94
00:03:38,880 --> 00:03:39,680
your neck.

95
00:03:42,710 --> 00:03:43,510
Feel that?

96
00:03:45,040 --> 00:03:47,620
Over time, the feeling stopped being rare.

97
00:03:48,320 --> 00:03:49,320
Every night.

98
00:03:49,700 --> 00:03:50,650
In the kitchen,

99
00:03:50,700 --> 00:03:51,760
opening the fridge.

100
00:03:51,960 --> 00:03:52,860
In the shower.

101
00:03:52,940 --> 00:03:54,020
Lying in bed.

102
00:03:54,970 --> 00:03:56,750
And the worst part wasn't feeling someone

103
00:03:56,800 --> 00:03:57,880
behind him.

104
00:03:58,560 --> 00:03:59,980
The worst part was feeling that,

105
00:04:00,030 --> 00:04:02,800
every night, it was a little closer.

106
00:04:04,250 --> 00:04:05,060
closer.

107
00:04:07,160 --> 00:04:08,940
He started hearing things.

108
00:04:09,240 --> 00:04:11,570
Footsteps in the hallway that stopped half

109
00:04:11,620 --> 00:04:13,340
a second after his own.

110
00:04:13,560 --> 00:04:16,090
Slow breathing, right after he turned off

111
00:04:16,140 --> 00:04:16,940
the light.

112
00:04:17,810 --> 00:04:19,350
Being a sound engineer,

113
00:04:19,400 --> 00:04:20,350
he did what he knew how to

114
00:04:20,400 --> 00:04:21,190
do.

115
00:04:21,240 --> 00:04:23,190
He left a professional microphone recording

116
00:04:23,240 --> 00:04:25,180
in the hallway all night long.

117
00:04:25,870 --> 00:04:26,680
In the morning,

118
00:04:26,730 --> 00:04:28,940
he put on his headphones and listened.

119
00:04:29,500 --> 00:04:30,800
Hours of silence.

120
00:04:31,140 --> 00:04:33,070
His own footsteps going to the bathroom,

121
00:04:33,120 --> 00:04:34,180
at two in the morning.

122
00:04:34,800 --> 00:04:37,040
And right after each of his steps…

123
00:04:37,620 --> 00:04:38,860
another step.

124
00:04:39,260 --> 00:04:40,140
Lighter.

125
00:04:40,380 --> 00:04:41,820
Half a second behind.

126
00:04:42,840 --> 00:04:45,080
He played that part about twenty times.

127
00:04:45,590 --> 00:04:47,300
Whenever he stopped in the hallway,

128
00:04:47,600 --> 00:04:49,540
the other footsteps stopped too.

129
00:04:50,360 --> 00:04:52,660
Except, the last time,

130
00:04:52,820 --> 00:04:54,190
after he had already gone back to

131
00:04:54,240 --> 00:04:55,040
bed…

132
00:04:55,420 --> 00:04:57,280
the footsteps kept going.

133
00:04:57,610 --> 00:04:58,580
Slowly.

134
00:04:59,120 --> 00:05:00,980
All the way to the bedroom door.

135
00:05:01,840 --> 00:05:03,060
He went to a doctor.

136
00:05:03,200 --> 00:05:04,420
Had tests done.

137
00:05:04,700 --> 00:05:06,000
Everything was normal.

138
00:05:06,320 --> 00:05:08,870
The doctor prescribed sleeping pills and said

139
00:05:08,920 --> 00:05:09,900
it was stress.

140
00:05:10,020 --> 00:05:10,940
Exhaustion.

141
00:05:11,620 --> 00:05:13,240
The pills made him sleep.

142
00:05:13,440 --> 00:05:14,950
But they didn't make the feeling go

143
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:15,800
away.

144
00:05:16,420 --> 00:05:17,770
It was on one of those sleepless

145
00:05:17,820 --> 00:05:19,830
nights that he found the study from

146
00:05:19,880 --> 00:05:20,740
Switzerland.

147
00:05:21,190 --> 00:05:23,360
And, for the first time in months,

148
00:05:23,520 --> 00:05:24,660
he felt relief.

149
00:05:25,140 --> 00:05:26,320
It was the brain.

150
00:05:26,440 --> 00:05:27,240
That's all.

151
00:05:27,320 --> 00:05:28,920
A half-second delay.

152
00:05:29,720 --> 00:05:30,950
For a few days,

153
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:31,820
it worked.

154
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:33,120
He slept better.

155
00:05:33,310 --> 00:05:35,110
He walked down the hallway without looking

156
00:05:35,160 --> 00:05:35,960
back.

157
00:05:36,620 --> 00:05:38,130
Until the night when,

158
00:05:38,180 --> 00:05:39,500
brushing his teeth,

159
00:05:39,680 --> 00:05:40,990
he felt the back of his neck

160
00:05:41,040 --> 00:05:42,160
go cold.

161
00:05:42,680 --> 00:05:43,880
It wasn't a shiver.

162
00:05:43,960 --> 00:05:45,280
It was cold.

163
00:05:45,490 --> 00:05:47,790
As if someone were breathing right there,

164
00:05:47,840 --> 00:05:49,260
inches away from him.

165
00:05:49,970 --> 00:05:51,220
He didn't turn around.

166
00:05:51,660 --> 00:05:52,850
For the first time,

167
00:05:52,900 --> 00:05:54,860
he was afraid to turn around.

168
00:05:55,960 --> 00:05:57,080
After that night,

169
00:05:57,160 --> 00:05:59,380
Rafael changed the whole apartment.

170
00:05:59,430 --> 00:06:01,170
He pushed all the furniture against the

171
00:06:01,220 --> 00:06:01,950
walls.

172
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:03,180
Left the lights on.

173
00:06:03,260 --> 00:06:04,390
Put mirrors in the corners,

174
00:06:04,440 --> 00:06:06,090
to see what was coming up behind

175
00:06:06,140 --> 00:06:06,940
him.

176
00:06:07,220 --> 00:06:09,200
And he started sleeping sitting up,

177
00:06:09,250 --> 00:06:10,620
with his back to the wall.

178
00:06:11,430 --> 00:06:13,340
But the feeling didn't go away.

179
00:06:13,580 --> 00:06:15,440
It just kept getting closer.

180
00:06:16,240 --> 00:06:18,690
One Sunday, his brother Lucas showed up

181
00:06:18,740 --> 00:06:19,720
unannounced.

182
00:06:20,140 --> 00:06:22,180
He thought the apartment looked strange.

183
00:06:22,640 --> 00:06:24,900
The furniture pressed against the walls,

184
00:06:25,260 --> 00:06:27,850
the mirrors, the lights on in broad

185
00:06:27,900 --> 00:06:28,820
daylight.

186
00:06:29,730 --> 00:06:31,340
Rafael tried to explain.

187
00:06:31,900 --> 00:06:34,340
Lucas laughed, a little awkwardly.

188
00:06:34,650 --> 00:06:36,100
Said he needed some sleep,

189
00:06:36,270 --> 00:06:37,270
needed to get out,

190
00:06:37,320 --> 00:06:38,180
see people.

191
00:06:39,030 --> 00:06:40,020
On his way out,

192
00:06:40,140 --> 00:06:41,420
halfway down the hallway,

193
00:06:41,890 --> 00:06:42,900
Lucas stopped.

194
00:06:43,570 --> 00:06:45,000
He rubbed the back of his neck.

195
00:06:45,980 --> 00:06:46,780
Man…

196
00:06:47,390 --> 00:06:49,300
where is this draft coming from?

197
00:06:50,470 --> 00:06:51,740
Rafael didn't answer.

198
00:06:52,300 --> 00:06:53,620
He just opened the door.

199
00:06:54,210 --> 00:06:55,900
And waited for his brother to leave.

200
00:06:57,300 --> 00:06:58,720
One sleepless night,

201
00:06:58,870 --> 00:07:00,830
he posted on an internet forum.

202
00:07:01,160 --> 00:07:02,940
He asked if anyone else felt it.

203
00:07:03,310 --> 00:07:05,120
Someone walking behind them,

204
00:07:05,460 --> 00:07:07,300
a little closer every night.

205
00:07:08,490 --> 00:07:11,400
Within hours, dozens of replies came in.

206
00:07:11,600 --> 00:07:13,220
People from all over Brazil.

207
00:07:13,510 --> 00:07:14,600
From other countries.

208
00:07:15,080 --> 00:07:17,380
Everyone describing the same thing.

209
00:07:18,360 --> 00:07:20,020
One reply caught his eye.

210
00:07:20,360 --> 00:07:21,950
A user who signed only with his

211
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:22,920
initials.

212
00:07:23,320 --> 00:07:24,450
He said he had found a way

213
00:07:24,500 --> 00:07:25,590
to prove it.

214
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:27,090
That he would take photos of his

215
00:07:27,140 --> 00:07:29,640
home every night and compare them.

216
00:07:30,380 --> 00:07:33,130
Rafael replied, asking him to share whatever

217
00:07:33,180 --> 00:07:34,770
he found.

218
00:07:35,150 --> 00:07:36,360
Three days later,

219
00:07:36,630 --> 00:07:38,400
one last message arrived.

220
00:07:39,200 --> 00:07:40,900
Just one sentence.

221
00:07:42,190 --> 00:07:43,980
Don't look for her.

222
00:07:45,320 --> 00:07:48,620
After that, the account never replied again.

223
00:07:51,070 --> 00:07:54,110
A little curiosity,

224
00:07:54,370 --> 00:07:55,310
since we're here.

225
00:07:56,340 --> 00:07:58,080
Each of your eyes has a blind

226
00:07:58,130 --> 00:07:58,950
spot.

227
00:07:59,090 --> 00:08:01,240
A place where the optic nerve leaves

228
00:08:01,290 --> 00:08:02,910
the eye, and where you,

229
00:08:02,960 --> 00:08:06,190
quite literally, can't see anything.

230
00:08:07,080 --> 00:08:08,160
You never notice it.

231
00:08:08,490 --> 00:08:10,440
Because your brain paints over that hole

232
00:08:10,490 --> 00:08:12,870
with whatever it thinks should be there.

233
00:08:13,990 --> 00:08:14,910
In other words…

234
00:08:15,430 --> 00:08:17,480
it hides from you what you can't

235
00:08:17,530 --> 00:08:18,330
see.

236
00:08:19,390 --> 00:08:20,310
Remember that.

237
00:08:21,660 --> 00:08:23,400
When we're afraid of something we can't

238
00:08:23,450 --> 00:08:24,250
see…

239
00:08:24,800 --> 00:08:25,730
what do we do?

240
00:08:26,510 --> 00:08:29,270
We try to prove it doesn't exist.

241
00:08:30,520 --> 00:08:33,270
That's exactly what Rafael decided to do.

242
00:08:33,970 --> 00:08:36,770
Every night, he started photographing the apartment.

243
00:08:37,220 --> 00:08:38,250
Every room.

244
00:08:38,430 --> 00:08:40,650
Same angle, same time.

245
00:08:41,640 --> 00:08:42,830
The idea was simple.

246
00:08:43,340 --> 00:08:44,830
If the photos showed nothing,

247
00:08:44,970 --> 00:08:46,810
the feeling was all in his head.

248
00:08:46,890 --> 00:08:49,350
And he could finally forget about it.

249
00:08:50,770 --> 00:08:51,990
Weeks went by.

250
00:08:52,350 --> 00:08:53,650
Hundreds of photos.

251
00:08:55,070 --> 00:08:57,020
One night, he printed them all and

252
00:08:57,070 --> 00:08:58,590
spread them out on the table.

253
00:08:59,280 --> 00:09:00,750
To look at them calmly.

254
00:09:00,890 --> 00:09:02,760
To prove, once and for all,

255
00:09:02,810 --> 00:09:04,590
that there was nothing there.

256
00:09:05,940 --> 00:09:07,310
And for a long time…

257
00:09:07,710 --> 00:09:08,570
there wasn't.

258
00:09:09,940 --> 00:09:11,400
Until he stopped at a photo of

259
00:09:11,450 --> 00:09:12,290
the street.

260
00:09:12,650 --> 00:09:13,780
Way in the back,

261
00:09:13,830 --> 00:09:15,590
past the last streetlight,

262
00:09:15,780 --> 00:09:17,210
between two trees.

263
00:09:17,930 --> 00:09:19,270
A shape.

264
00:09:19,780 --> 00:09:20,580
Tall.

265
00:09:20,810 --> 00:09:21,790
Too thin.

266
00:09:22,290 --> 00:09:23,510
Standing still.

267
00:09:24,950 --> 00:09:26,390
He picked up the next photo.

268
00:09:26,650 --> 00:09:27,540
The living room.

269
00:09:27,860 --> 00:09:28,730
And he looked.

270
00:09:29,440 --> 00:09:30,530
There it was.

271
00:09:30,830 --> 00:09:32,810
In the reflection on the window.

272
00:09:33,410 --> 00:09:34,350
In the hallway.

273
00:09:35,010 --> 00:09:36,390
In the kitchen doorway.

274
00:09:37,140 --> 00:09:38,870
In the corner of the bedroom.

275
00:09:39,750 --> 00:09:41,670
In every one.

276
00:09:42,380 --> 00:09:44,130
And in each photo…

277
00:09:44,940 --> 00:09:46,230
a little closer.

278
00:09:47,360 --> 00:09:49,530
in every one.

279
00:09:51,430 --> 00:09:53,630
Rafael picked up a red pen.

280
00:09:53,860 --> 00:09:55,300
And, with a shaking hand,

281
00:09:55,350 --> 00:09:57,090
he circled each one.

282
00:09:58,180 --> 00:09:59,230
When he was done,

283
00:09:59,950 --> 00:10:02,500
he understood the most terrifying thing of

284
00:10:02,550 --> 00:10:03,350
all.

285
00:10:04,970 --> 00:10:06,670
It had never been a feeling.

286
00:10:07,450 --> 00:10:08,930
It was someone.

287
00:10:09,930 --> 00:10:11,570
It always had been.

288
00:10:12,360 --> 00:10:14,580
And only then did he remember his

289
00:10:14,630 --> 00:10:15,530
grandmother.

290
00:10:16,120 --> 00:10:17,250
If you don't look,

291
00:10:17,410 --> 00:10:18,530
you won't find.

292
00:10:19,110 --> 00:10:20,430
He had looked.

293
00:10:20,900 --> 00:10:22,770
Three forty in the morning.

294
00:10:25,380 --> 00:10:27,230
That's when he recorded the message for

295
00:10:27,280 --> 00:10:28,080
his brother.

296
00:10:31,810 --> 00:10:33,640
I found her.

297
00:10:33,800 --> 00:10:37,300
She's in every single photo.

298
00:10:38,060 --> 00:10:40,420
And she knows that I know.

299
00:10:42,220 --> 00:10:44,910
After that, Rafael did the only thing

300
00:10:44,960 --> 00:10:46,090
left to do.

301
00:10:46,140 --> 00:10:48,010
He opened the front camera on his

302
00:10:48,060 --> 00:10:48,670
phone.

303
00:10:48,720 --> 00:10:50,730
And, without turning his body,

304
00:10:50,780 --> 00:10:52,610
he looked at the hallway behind him

305
00:10:52,660 --> 00:10:53,640
on the screen.

306
00:10:54,450 --> 00:10:55,820
She was right there.

307
00:10:56,320 --> 00:10:57,970
One step behind him.

308
00:10:58,210 --> 00:10:59,820
At the height of his face.

309
00:11:00,630 --> 00:11:01,940
And, for the first time,

310
00:11:02,560 --> 00:11:04,240
she wasn't standing still.

311
00:11:06,360 --> 00:11:08,590
The phone fell to the hallway floor.

312
00:11:08,640 --> 00:11:10,660
And kept recording.

313
00:11:11,510 --> 00:11:12,310
The ceiling.

314
00:11:12,920 --> 00:11:14,220
The light bulb swinging.

315
00:11:14,940 --> 00:11:16,360
His slippers on the floor.

316
00:11:18,020 --> 00:11:18,880
No sound.

317
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:20,880
No scream.

318
00:11:22,370 --> 00:11:23,740
Just the empty hallway.

319
00:11:24,630 --> 00:11:26,160
Lucas arrived in the morning.

320
00:11:26,580 --> 00:11:28,600
The door was locked from the inside.

321
00:11:28,920 --> 00:11:30,600
The windows, shut.

322
00:11:31,140 --> 00:11:33,140
The phone, on the hallway floor.

323
00:11:33,580 --> 00:11:35,800
The battery, almost dead.

324
00:11:36,360 --> 00:11:38,420
And on the living room table,

325
00:11:39,090 --> 00:11:40,280
dozens of photos.

326
00:11:40,990 --> 00:11:42,860
Each one with a red circle.

327
00:11:44,550 --> 00:11:46,620
Rafael's case became a statistic.

328
00:11:47,240 --> 00:11:48,010
In Brazil alone,

329
00:11:48,060 --> 00:11:49,650
in twenty twenty-five,

330
00:11:49,730 --> 00:11:51,550
more than eighty-four thousand people went

331
00:11:51,600 --> 00:11:52,400
missing.

332
00:11:52,960 --> 00:11:54,360
Most of them are found.

333
00:11:55,230 --> 00:11:56,030
Some…

334
00:11:56,740 --> 00:11:57,560
never are.

335
00:11:58,590 --> 00:12:01,020
The scientists were right about one thing.

336
00:12:01,980 --> 00:12:03,720
There really is a delay.

337
00:12:04,560 --> 00:12:05,690
It's just not in your brain.

338
00:12:05,740 --> 00:12:09,460
She was in the images all along.

339
00:12:09,960 --> 00:12:11,200
From the very beginning.

340
00:12:11,990 --> 00:12:13,800
Throughout this entire video…

341
00:12:14,300 --> 00:12:16,220
she was in every single scene.

342
00:12:16,940 --> 00:12:18,180
Right in front of you.

343
00:12:18,880 --> 00:12:19,920
And neither you…

344
00:12:20,460 --> 00:12:21,420
nor Rafael…

345
00:12:22,230 --> 00:12:23,140
ever noticed.

346
00:12:24,340 --> 00:12:26,860
On the street.

347
00:12:28,840 --> 00:12:30,280
In the window.

348
00:12:32,650 --> 00:12:34,360
At the end of the hallway.

349
00:12:36,650 --> 00:12:38,180
In the kitchen doorway.

350
00:12:40,300 --> 00:12:42,500
In the corner of the bedroom.

351
00:12:44,660 --> 00:12:46,740
Behind the shower curtain.

352
00:12:48,770 --> 00:12:50,820
In the middle of the hallway.

353
00:12:53,260 --> 00:12:54,980
Right behind him.

354
00:12:56,020 --> 00:12:57,520
If you don't believe me…

355
00:12:58,190 --> 00:12:59,560
go back to the beginning.

356
00:13:00,270 --> 00:13:01,080
And look.

357
00:13:02,120 --> 00:13:03,820
Now you know where to look.

358
00:13:04,560 --> 00:13:07,720
Rafael didn't disappear because she got close.

359
00:13:08,500 --> 00:13:11,740
He disappeared because he found out.

360
00:13:12,560 --> 00:13:13,400
And you…

361
00:13:14,150 --> 00:13:16,400
just saw the same photos he did.

362
00:13:17,520 --> 00:13:18,320
Good night.

363
00:13:19,080 --> 00:13:21,300
And when this video ends…

364
00:13:22,150 --> 00:13:24,040
don't look behind you.
